                <pb facs="0849" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.796/184: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-06T09:00:00-05:00">July 6, 1940—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. The Department’s telegram No. 87 was presented in accordance with the
                    Department’s instructions and the general outline was accepted in principle with
                    the exception of points mentioned below, also that the elimination of Sedta must
                    be undertaken by Panagra, in which the Ecuadoran Government will collaborate.
                    That is, Panagra <pb facs="0850" n="838" xml:id="pg838"/> will provide three
                    international services weekly, with the fourth via Esmeraldas, Cali and
                    Cristóbal, also serve in Ecuador all points now reached by Sedta immediately
                    ground facilities are avialable. Ecuadoran Government desires Panagra services
                    completely planned before actually putting on pressure to eliminate Sedta.
                    Ecuador has the service now satisfactory for Sedta but fields at Loja, Cuenca
                    and possibly Manta will need amplification for Douglasses while they are
                    satisfactory for Junkers. Any improvement required for Panagra type planes to be
                    undertaken by Panagra.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
